===Climate===
[[File:Kofu Oyster Beds.jpg|thumb|left|250px|The oyster beds of Kofu Bay at low tide, revealing the cultivation infrastructure.]]

Kofu Prefecture experiences a humid subtropical climate (Köppen classification Cfa) strongly moderated by the maritime influence of Kofu Bay. The sheltered bay creates a microclimate characterized by milder temperatures and higher humidity than the surrounding coastal regions. The calm waters of the bay also reduce the impact of the seasonal typhoons that affect more exposed prefectures, making Kofu's aquaculture operations unusually stable.

The winter months bring the celebrated {{nihongo|'''Kaki Season'''|牡蠣の季節|Kaki no Kisetsu}}, when the cold ocean temperatures produce oysters at their peak—plump, creamy, and intensely flavored. The engawa harvest peaks in the spring, when flatfish move into the shallow waters to spawn.

As illustrated by the climate data for the capital city below, the region is characterized by warm, humid conditions year-round with substantial precipitation. The bay's sheltering effect is evident in the reduced wind speeds and the extended growing season for the hillside citrus groves.

